  "description": "PITTIX crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H84 Gd3 N8 Ni2 O16 1+,3(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1,Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.217-3.892 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.76-114.56°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni2Gd3(LH)4]Cl·3CH3OH·H2O.",
